WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.130
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Grammar, level A two.

2
00:00:05.430 --> 00:00:08.375
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:08.675 --> 00:00:14.102
Unit thirty-seven: Be Able To. Today you will talk about ability in different tenses.

4
00:00:14.402 --> 00:00:16.996
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:17.933 --> 00:00:21.004
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:21.850 --> 00:00:22.990
Be able to.

7
00:00:23.983 --> 00:00:27.121
Be able to means to have the skill or chance to do something.

8
00:00:27.717 --> 00:00:28.950
I am able to swim.

9
00:00:29.550 --> 00:00:31.831
Your turn. Say: Be able to.

10
00:00:34.667 --> 00:00:35.621
Be able to.

11
00:00:36.383 --> 00:00:37.373
Was able to.

12
00:00:38.383 --> 00:00:41.532
Was able to means had the skill or chance in the past.

13
00:00:42.117 --> 00:00:43.780
She was able to finish.

14
00:00:44.383 --> 00:00:46.885
Your turn. Say: Was able to.

15
00:00:49.733 --> 00:00:50.874
Was able to.

16
00:00:51.617 --> 00:00:52.722
Will be able to.

17
00:00:53.717 --> 00:00:56.982
Will be able to means will have the skill or chance in the future.

18
00:00:57.583 --> 00:00:59.037
We will be able to travel.

19
00:00:59.650 --> 00:01:02.291
Your turn. Say: Will be able to.

20
00:01:05.133 --> 00:01:06.610
Will be able to.

21
00:01:07.350 --> 00:01:08.398
Ability.

22
00:01:09.383 --> 00:01:11.870
Ability means the skill to do something.

23
00:01:12.483 --> 00:01:14.622
Ability grows with practice.

24
00:01:15.217 --> 00:01:17.556
Your turn. Say: Ability.

25
00:01:20.400 --> 00:01:21.401
Ability.

26
00:01:22.150 --> 00:01:23.198
Manage to.

27
00:01:24.183 --> 00:01:27.297
Manage to means to succeed in doing something difficult.

28
00:01:27.883 --> 00:01:29.477
I managed to finish.

29
00:01:30.083 --> 00:01:32.538
Your turn. Say: Manage to.

30
00:01:35.400 --> 00:01:36.657
Manage to.

31
00:01:37.417 --> 00:01:38.186
Can't.

32
00:01:39.183 --> 00:01:40.742
Can't means not able to.

33
00:01:41.350 --> 00:01:42.769
I can't swim.

34
00:01:43.383 --> 00:01:46.082
Your turn. Say: Can't.

35
00:01:48.933 --> 00:01:49.633
Can't.

36
00:01:50.383 --> 00:01:51.117
Couldn't.

37
00:01:52.117 --> 00:01:53.849
Couldn't means was not able to.

38
00:01:54.450 --> 00:01:55.579
I couldn't come.

39
00:01:56.183 --> 00:01:58.418
Your turn. Say: Couldn't.

40
00:02:01.267 --> 00:02:02.012
Couldn't.

41
00:02:02.750 --> 00:02:04.041
Future ability.

42
00:02:05.050 --> 00:02:08.060
Future ability means what we will be able to do later.

43
00:02:08.650 --> 00:02:10.650
Study will give you future ability.

44
00:02:11.250 --> 00:02:14.135
Your turn. Say: Future ability.

45
00:02:17.000 --> 00:02:18.315
Future ability.

46
00:02:19.100 --> 00:02:22.925
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:23.783 --> 00:02:27.899
Visal, can you swim? And will you be able to swim better next year?

48
00:02:28.983 --> 00:02:37.951
I can swim now, and I will be able to swim better next year. Be able to means the same as can, but it works in more tenses.

49
00:02:39.050 --> 00:02:40.388
What are the forms?

50
00:02:41.483 --> 00:02:56.079
Present: am, is or are able to. Past: was or were able to. Future: will be able to. After able to, we use the base verb: She was able to finish. We cannot say will can.

51
00:02:57.183 --> 00:02:58.788
Can and could for the past?

52
00:02:59.883 --> 00:03:12.186
Could is for general ability in the past: I could swim when I was six. For one specific success, we use was able to: I was able to finish yesterday. Couldn't is fine for both.

53
00:03:13.333 --> 00:03:14.927
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:15.783 --> 00:03:19.803
Grammar focus: Ability: be able to plus base verb.

55
00:03:20.103 --> 00:03:21.371
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:22.083 --> 00:03:24.106
I am able to swim very well.

57
00:03:25.017 --> 00:03:27.016
She was able to finish the test.

58
00:03:27.917 --> 00:03:29.916
We will be able to travel next year.

59
00:03:30.867 --> 00:03:39.884
Use am / is / are able to, was / were able to and will be able to. Use could for general past ability and was able to for one success. Never say will can.

60
00:03:40.650 --> 00:03:43.662
Be careful! Don't say: I will can come tomorrow.

61
00:03:45.600 --> 00:03:48.041
Say: I will be able to come tomorrow.

62
00:03:48.341 --> 00:03:50.178
Use will be able to for the future.

63
00:03:50.967 --> 00:03:53.491
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:03:54.300 --> 00:03:56.067
What Will You Be Able to Do?.

65
00:03:56.367 --> 00:03:59.690
I am able to swim, and I will be able to dive next year.

66
00:04:00.700 --> 00:04:03.524
Yesterday I was able to finish my homework early.

67
00:04:04.533 --> 00:04:06.428
When I was six, I could ride a bike.

68
00:04:07.433 --> 00:04:09.340
He couldn't come because he was ill.

69
00:04:10.333 --> 00:04:12.704
Practice improves your future ability.

70
00:04:13.800 --> 00:04:17.697
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:18.550 --> 00:04:20.851
Next year I blank speak English better.

72
00:04:21.151 --> 00:04:25.037
A, will can. B, will be able to. C, am can.

73
00:04:28.600 --> 00:04:30.762
The answer is B: will be able to.

74
00:04:31.917 --> 00:04:34.288
Yesterday she blank finish the test.

75
00:04:34.588 --> 00:04:38.624
A, was able to. B, will be able to. C, is able to.

76
00:04:42.167 --> 00:04:44.155
The answer is A: was able to.

77
00:04:45.317 --> 00:04:47.618
When I was six, I blank swim.

78
00:04:47.918 --> 00:04:51.374
A, could. B, will can. C, am able.

79
00:04:54.933 --> 00:04:57.003
The answer is A: could.

80
00:04:58.150 --> 00:04:59.766
Which sentence is correct?

81
00:05:00.066 --> 00:05:05.043
A, I will can come.. B, I will be able to come.. C, I will able to come..

82
00:05:08.600 --> 00:05:11.435
The answer is B: I will be able to come..

83
00:05:12.583 --> 00:05:15.070
According to the reading, why couldn't he come?

84
00:05:15.370 --> 00:05:19.546
A, he was ill. B, he was busy. C, he was late.

85
00:05:23.100 --> 00:05:25.309
The answer is A: he was ill.

86
00:05:26.500 --> 00:05:29.559
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:05:30.417 --> 00:05:32.370
What will you be able to do next year?

88
00:05:41.183 --> 00:05:42.626
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:05:42.926 --> 00:05:53.487
Next year I will be able to speak English more fluently. I will also be able to read longer books. I use will be able to because can does not have a future form.

90
00:05:53.787 --> 00:05:55.554
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:05:56.450 --> 00:06:01.831
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and ability: be able to plus base verb.

92
00:06:02.131 --> 00:06:06.153
Today's value is ambition. Dream big and work hard for your future.

93
00:06:06.453 --> 00:06:09.814
See you in Unit thirty-eight. Goodbye!

94
00:06:10.114 --> 00:06:12.522
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

